Greeting people as they join. Our own join triggers on JOIN too, like
mIRC; the me prefix makes an event only for our own.

-- greet.mrc --
on *:JOIN:#:{
  if ($nick == $me) {
    echo $chan Now talking in $chan
    return
  }
  msg $chan Welcome to $chan $+ , $nick $+ !
}
on me:*:PART:#:echo -s Left $chan
on !*:PART:#:echo $chan $nick left ( $+ $1- $+ )
; With no window, an event's /echo goes to the network's status window, like
; mIRC (checked in mIRC: the help doesn't say).
on *:TEXT:!echotest:#:echo from the event
-- transcript --
me trout
active #elsewhere
< :trout!t@host JOIN #trout
= #trout: Now talking in #trout
< :bob!b@host JOIN #trout
> /msg #trout Welcome to #trout, bob!
< :bob!b@host PART #trout :see you
= #trout: bob left (see you)
< :trout!t@host PART #trout
= status: Left #trout
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG #trout :!echotest
= status: from the event
